# API test conventions

## 1. Sources of truth

A **specification or approved doc** is documented; a row in `api/CATALOG.md` is **observed**; anything else is an **assumption** and belongs under **Not yet tested**. Tests from observed rows are **characterization** tests (pin today’s behavior); tests from a spec are **contract** tests.

✅ **Good** — constants and shapes trace to a catalog row marked `executed`:

```typescript
/** Values recorded in api/CATALOG.md (2026-10-16 API test pass). */
export const CATALOG_GET_AUTH_STATUS = 200;
// … expectMeResponse asserts fields listed for GET /api/v1/me in CATALOG.md
```

❌ **Bad** — exercise a route with no catalog row and no spec citation; leave it listed instead:

```markdown
## Not yet tested
- **Write endpoints not hit on this pass** — … playdate propose/respond/cancel …
```

## 2. Requests

Base URL comes from Playwright `baseURL` (`APP_URL`). Authenticated and anonymous contexts only from `api/fixtures.ts` (`mainApi`, `altApi`, `anonApi`), which reuse `support/api-client.ts`. Never a token, full URL, or hardcoded id in a spec.

✅ **Good** — `me.api.spec.ts`:

```typescript
const PATH = '/api/v1/me';

test('GET /api/v1/me returns catalog status, content type, and shape @api', async ({ mainApi }) => {
  const response = await mainApi.get(PATH);
```

❌ **Bad** — bypass fixtures and embed secrets or origins:

```typescript
const response = await request.get('https://test.buddytime.ca/api/v1/me', {
  headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer eyJ…' },
});
```

## 3. Two tests per endpoint

Per endpoint: one **success** test and one **intentional error** test that changes **exactly one** thing (drop token, omit a required field, empty body). Assert status and fields you actually expect; ensure nothing sensitive leaks in the body.

✅ **Good** — `availability.api.spec.ts` pair; anon case only removes auth via `anonApi`:

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/availability returns catalog status, content type, and shape @api', async ({ mainApi }) => { … });
test('GET /api/v1/availability without token returns catalog status @api', async ({ anonApi }) => {
  await expectCatalogUnauthenticatedGet(anonApi, PATH);
});
```

❌ **Bad** — one test, two failures at once, or guessing status/shape not in catalog:

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/availability errors @api', async ({ anonApi }) => {
  const response = await anonApi.get(PATH, { headers: { Accept: 'text/plain' } });
  expect(response.status()).toBe(403);
  expect(await response.text()).toContain('bt_token');
});
```

## 4. Writes

Write only when **undo is documented or observed** (catalog row + known DELETE/status). Call `trackRecord` immediately after create so cleanup runs even if the test fails later.

✅ **Good** — `children.api.spec.ts` after `POST /api/v1/children` (catalog: 201 + `DELETE` 204):

```typescript
const createResponse = await mainApi.post(CHILDREN_PATH, { data: payload });
expect(createResponse.status()).toBe(CATALOG_CREATE_STATUS);
const createdRecord = created as { id: string };
trackRecord({ type: 'child', id: createdRecord.id, owner: recordOwner });
```

❌ **Bad** — create without tracking or without a catalog-backed delete path:

```typescript
await mainApi.post('/api/v1/children', { data: payload });
// no trackRecord; no documented DELETE cleanup
```

## 5. Tags

Exactly **one** tag per test: `@api`. Not on `describe()`.

✅ **Good**:

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/me without token returns catalog status @api', async ({ anonApi }) => {
```

❌ **Bad**:

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/me @smoke @api', async ({ mainApi }) => {
```

## 6. Evidence

Label every claim **executed**, **inspected only**, or **not yet tested**. A status or body copied from a spec, chat, or agent prediction is **not** evidence until observed or run.

✅ **Good** — catalog table and helper comment:

```markdown
| GET | `/api/v1/me` | … | 200 | … | yes | executed |
```

```typescript
/** Values recorded in api/CATALOG.md (2026-10-16 API test pass). */
```

❌ **Bad** — assert or document without a label:

```typescript
// OpenAPI says 404 when community missing — not run yet
expect(response.status()).toBe(404);
```
